// RT-61's family (0.30.2), the outer-loop vectorizer: lanes over j, each
// lane's scan down column j stored at every row, and a second sum over
// the running value. Each lane is one j, computed in the scalar order, so
// a scan is exact there (no lane holds part of another's value); the
// columns 0, 1, the vector width and one either side, and more. The output
// is rustc's.
// EXPECT: colscan_i8_0 0 0
// EXPECT: colsum2_i8_0 0 0
// EXPECT: colscan_i8_1 8793758778014808209 12409753524017129366
// EXPECT: colsum2_i8_1 8793758778014808209 17312939373442621623
